{"id": "EUVD-2026-106151", "enisaUuid": "de21fef0-1751-38ef-aa28-1e481115281a", "description": "Vulnerability in the MySQL Server, MySQL Cluster product of Oracle MySQL (component: Server: Clone Plugin).  Supported versions that are affected are MySQL Server: 8.4.0-8.4.12, 9.7.0-9.7.3, 26.7.0-26.7.1; MySQL Cluster: 8.0.0-8.0.49, 8.4.0-8.4.12, 9.7.0-9.7.3 and  26.7.0-26.7.1. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows high privileged attacker with network access via multiple protocols to compromise MySQL Server, MySQL Cluster.  Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in unauthorized ability to cause a hang or frequently repeatable crash (complete DOS) of MySQL Server, MySQL Cluster. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 4.9 (Availability impacts).  CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H).", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T21:22:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T17:32:34", "baseScore": 4.9, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpuoct2026.html"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7836-p73q-68fx", "CVE-2026-101750"], "assigner": "oracle", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7c2f0f0d-3788-3e79-b086-6ba895ba5910", "product": {"name": "MySQL Cluster", "vendor": {"name": "Oracle Corporation"}}, "product_version": "9.7.0-9.7.3"}, {"id": "90be9fcc-6d0e-3e37-bb0a-363541962f74", "product": {"name": "MySQL Cluster", "vendor": {"name": "Oracle Corporation"}}, "product_version": "8.0.0-8.0.49"}, {"id": "9b738d2c-e16a-3a1b-8ca9-111638a1c769", "product": {"name": "MySQL Server", "vendor": {"name": "Oracle Corporation"}}, "product_version": "26.7.0-26.7.1"}, {"id": "c6e4a590-31d6-3f8a-90d3-3264e8b65dd1", "product": {"name": "MySQL Server", "vendor": {"name": "Oracle Corporation"}}, "product_version": "8.4.0-8.4.12"}, {"id": "e4552068-fd08-364a-b757-da4e0e8c3c0e", "product": {"name": "MySQL Cluster", "vendor": {"name": "Oracle Corporation"}}, "product_version": "26.7.0-26.7.1"}, {